      "reason_rejected": "This option treats the idiom as a statement of magical causality (counting prevents hatching), which is factually incorrect and not the intended meaning of the proverb."
    },
    {
      "answer": "F",
      "reason_rejected": "This option describes the potential negative outcome of the *mistake* (relying on the chickens), but the question asks what happens *if you count them*. Counting itself does not guarantee you end up without chickens; they might still hatch."
    }
